## UI Grouping

- Skills (scan)
- Custom commands (scan)
- Agents (scan)
- Built-ins (hardcoded list w/ handlers)

## Architecture

Hook-per-source pattern holds: each registry feeds one `AutocompleteMenu`. `ChatPanel.onKeyDown` iterates hooks first-returns-true. For 4+ hooks, move to explicit priority ordering.

## Suggested Order

1. **Custom commands** — reuses 80% of skills code (fs scan, frontmatter parse, autocomplete hook)
2. **/clear** — cheap, high user expectation
3. **Agents** — same pattern as skills/custom-cmds
4. **@file** — own hook, biggest UX shift
5. Built-ins that open settings/URLs (batch: `/config`, `/memory`, `/permissions`, `/hooks`, `/mcp`, `/bug`, `/release-notes`)
6. Data-driven built-ins (`/status`, `/cost`, `/help`)
7. Template injectors (`/init`, `/review`)
8. `/doctor`
